! vfl_index_store_decode.strap -- AFTER A VFL STORE INTO INDEX STORAGE,
! THE NEXT INSTRUCTION IS DECODED ONLY WHEN THE NEW INDEX CONTENTS HAS
! ARRIVED.  Built 2026-11-17 with StretchCore's redecodeAfterHold
! (docs/atlas_oracle.md, "Closing the residuals" item 12).
!
! THE SOURCE.  Perf. Char. Vol. 1 printed p.3-21 (PDF 39, read in the
! image): "A store into index storage is a time-consuming operation.
! Whenever such an instruction is decoded, since the next instruction
! may make use of the new index contents, the I-box does no further
! decoding until the new index contents arrives."  Perf. Char. Vol. 2 PDF
! 124 (ST, no forwarding) prints the I-BOX column ($X0-$X3) 16.2 clocks
! over EXTERNL, and 2 more indexed.
!
! THE BODY.  Four ST(BU,64,8) into $X1, four more indexed by $X5 (= 0),
! then the value is read back from $X1 by a VFL L and stored in RES.
!
! MEASURED, 2026-11-17 (CYCLES in run_tests.sh's run line).
!   the model as of this deck .......................... CYCLES 550
!   OBSERVED INJECTION, reverted from a saved copy checked with cmp:
!   - the redecode arm in rl_prepare removed ............ CYCLES 446
!   Nothing else failed (PC and RES pass).
! The control is decks/vfl_internal_operand.strap (no store into index
! storage), whose CYCLES (552) did not move under the injection.

        SLC, (8)2000.0

START   LX, $X5, ZERO
        L(BU,64,8), VAL
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1($X5)
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1($X5)
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1($X5)
        ST(BU,64,8), $X1($X5)
        L(BU,64,8), ZERO
        L(BU,64,8), $X1
        ST(BU,64,8), RES

PASS    BEW, $

        SLC, (8)2200.0

VAL     DD(BU,64,8), (16)0123456789ABCDEF
ZERO    DD(BU,64,8), 0
RES     DD(BU,64,8), 0

        END, START
